I've found that, as a monk, cats and dogs are more trouble that
they're worth.  If you don't have a magic whistle you'll starve to
death trying to get them to follow you up/down stairs.  Whenever I
find a polymorph tray I bait them in.  If they turn into a pudding, so
what, just abandon them.

The last time I did this I got a silver dragon.  He killed everything
there.  It was a bummer not being able to buy AC but the spellbooks
were handy.  I took him back to all the other shops and priests and
did the same.

I didn't notice anything bad happening to me.  Could the gods be
pissed and I be missing it?

